WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.901
-Welcome to the show.
I am such a fan.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.634
-Oh, thank you.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.534
-I love this.
-Can I just tell you something?

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:11.300
I just -- I very recently saw a
really wonderful clip of you

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.701
and the late and absolutely
great Olivia Newton-John.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:15.801
-Whoo!
-Right?

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:17.100
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.901
-She's such an icon in
Australia, and I just adore her.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.167
And you were singing
"The One that I Want"

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:25.067
from "Grease," which was
basically my childhood fantasy

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.334
that you got to live.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:27.934
-That was totally impromptu,
by the way.

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.200
It was not planned.
-Seriously?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.300
-Yeah. Olivia Newton-John
was on the show,

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.567
and we were going to
commercial break or something.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.367
And The Roots
just started playing it,

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.901
and she grabbed the mic,

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:40.234
and just, as a pro would do,
she just started singing it.

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.167
And I was like, "Oh, my gosh.
I have to duet with her."

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.300
So like, "You're the one..."

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.033
Then she started doing
the dance.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.334
And I was like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.534
-You did great, though.

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.434
-I, like, started to cry.
I couldn't believe it.

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:50.701
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:53.234
-Well, I was crying watching it.
It was very moving.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.868
-Did you ever meet her?
-I did.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:59.200
Yeah, years ago, I did a
production of "The Boy From Oz,"

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.701
an Australian musical,

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:03.601
with another Australian icon,
Peter Allen.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.934
And I got to sing
"I Honestly Love You,"

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:08.534
which is a song
that Olivia made famous.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.067
And she came to
the show one night,

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:11.534
so I was, you know, terrified.

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:14.033
And she came back
after the show

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.501
and was, you know, just gorgeous
and gracious and kind.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.767
-She's unbelievable.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:21.067
Like, stunningly gorgeous, like,
amazingly talented,

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.200
and, like, just everything.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.467
I just -- Oh!

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:27.400
-She was just, you know,
a real kind of good person.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.167
So compassionate and kind
and just radiated that

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.534
in everything she did.

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:34.200
I mean, she's iconic in
Australia and beyond, I guess,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.300
but for us, she has a very
special place in our hearts.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.601
-Thanks for bringing that up,

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.767
'cause I love that clip
that we did that with her.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:40.834
It was amazing.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.868
-When you did
that play with Hugh,

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:46.834
did you ever think of like,
"Oh, yeah, I've done

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.968
enough plays where I go like,
'I deserve to be on this

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:50.367
giant Broadway production.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.767
This is a big deal now.'"

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.767
Or do you go, like --
You go back to those days

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:56.267
where you were like,
"I was playing a tree in a play,

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.367
and..."

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.534
-Did somebody tell you that?

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:01.701
I actually was playing
not a tree, but a hedge.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.501
-Wow! That's...

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.434
No, they did not -- I did not --

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:06.767
We all know you
from your hedge work.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.400
Yeah. I knew you were a tree.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.667
-That's what you were
clapping for, right?

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:12.501
-Yes. Oh, the hedge.
When did you play a hedge?

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.667
-Many years ago, Jimmy,
when I first moved to New York,

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.968
I was an extra at the Met Opera.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:18.901
-Wow! That's a big deal.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:21.434
-It was, actually.
Yeah, it was fantastic.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.100
I got to go out on that
incredible stage,

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.534
but dressed as a hedge.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.067
So, you know,
no one was seeing me,

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:29.534
but I was seeing them
through the leaves.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.133
-At the Met Opera?
-At the Met Opera.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.234
-I was thinking, like, this was,
like, a childhood --

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.167
if you were going back to that,
but you actually made it to --

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.300
That's big-time.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.968
-Yeah, I was a grown man
when I was doing it.

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.968
I know it sounds
childlike, but --

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.367
-Wow! So, the hedge --
Did the hedge move?

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.667
-Yes. I was one of six.

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.400
And we were -- I think it was
"Cosi fan tutte"

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.601
or something like that,

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.801
something that had
a garden scene, obviously.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.567
And we were --
You know, we were choreographed

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.501
and we had to,
like, sway to the music

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:56.734
and, you know --

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.133
-Congratulations.
I didn't even know.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.334
I did not know that.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:02.634
I just assumed
every actor plays a tree or...

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:05.000
-It's not on my résumé.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.734
Here you go from there
to Emmy nominee.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:10.667
Man, you crushed it with
"The White Lotus," crushed it.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:11.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:16.067
-I mean, that was honestly --
I could not wait --

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.200
Every time you were onscreen,
I go -- And what a cast.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.601
Everyone was great.
-Amazing. Yeah.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.501
-Everyone was great and everyone
knocked it out of the park.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.934
-It's one of those shows that is
a true ensemble, right?

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.868
Like, everybody gets
their moment to shine.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:27.801
And everybody just kind of rose
to the occasion

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:28.934
in such a beautiful way.

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.033
-But, man, oh, man.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.834
I mean, I was, like --

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.734
You were just knocking
the cover off the ball.

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:34.801
Home run after home run.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.067
Every episode, I'm like,

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.968
"I can't wait to see
what trouble you get into."

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:42.434
Your character was so good,
so rascally, so funny,

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.901
and just -- You just nailed it,
all the way.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:47.634
What an arc and the whole way --
If you haven't seen it,

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.033
please do yourself a favor
and watch "The White Lotus"

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.167
and watch Murray.

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:51.601
But it was just brilliant.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.100
And this was all done, like,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.300
during the pandemic, right?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.834
-Yeah. Yeah, early on.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:59.400
So there was very
little contact in the beginning.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.100
We just, you know,
sent in self tapes,

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:05.133
and then, you know,
we found out we got the job.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.834
And then we were whisked out
of our COVID caves

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:09.501
and taken to Hawaii.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:12.868
-But, I mean, Mike White
kind of wrote it and filmed it

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:15.434
in like two months
or three months.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:17.701
-Yeah, he wrote those -- I mean,
they were incredible scripts,

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:20.567
and they barely changed as
we started working on the show,

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:21.567
'cause they were so tight.

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.067
And he wrote them in two months.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.267
And, you know,
then we started shooting,

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:27.868
shot it in four months,
and it was all over.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.000
-I also want to
mention you're in

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.300
Season 2 of "Physical"
on Apple TV+.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.100
-Rose Byrne, we love.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.267
-Oh, my gosh.
She's such a legend.

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.400
-Oh, she is fantastic.
-And a wonderful person.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.501
-You play Vinnie Green.
-I do.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:48.767
-You are a --
Well, this is you in action.

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:49.934
-Look at those knees.

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.868
-Yeah, how would you
describe those knees?

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.634
How would you describe
your character?

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:55.534
Who -- Is it based on anyone?
Is it --

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:58.834
-I mean, it's sort of loosely
based on Richard Simmons

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.200
and those kind of fitness sort
of gurus of the time.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.467
-Yeah.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.701
-Sort of leaning into
the fitness guru that then

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.934
kind of took a real
sort of personal touch

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:10.267
and really connects with his
audience in a very personal way,

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.167
like Richard Simmons did.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:13.601
-You know, it's so funny,
'cause you watch it,

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:16.767
and you're like "Wow, these
people are really energetic."

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.868
-Yeah, over the top.
Just say it.

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.634
-Yeah.
I mean, really over the top.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:23.067
And you're like, "Wow,
this is such a great character."

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.801
But you realize,
if you grew up --

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:27.000
this is actually how
everyone acted.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.601
Like, "You got a..."

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:31.434
And you go, "Wow!
This is -- Oh, my gosh.

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:32.968
I'm exhausted just by
you talking."

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.467
-Right. Yeah, yeah. Exactly.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.634
I mean, when I got the scripts,
you know, it reads on the page

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:39.234
as very over the top,
some of the stuff we did,

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:41.634
like an infomercial
and, you know,

00:05:41.634 --> 00:05:46.767
my first aerobics class that I
had to take was to "Proud Mary,"

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:48.567
this very kind of,
you know, upbeat number.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.734
And it's all sort of
such high energy.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.501
But then you go back
and watch these videos

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:57.067
of people like Richard Simmons,
and it is kind of crazy.

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:59.167
In a great way, I mean,
but it's so over the top.

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:00.601
-But it's real.
-Yeah, yeah, its real.

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:01.901
-You're very good in that.

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:05.033
And, once again, congratulations
on "The White Lotus."

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:07.434
Man, oh, man, please come back.
I am a giant fan.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.734
I want to show everyone a clip.
-Thanks for having me.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.901
-Here is Murray Bartlett in
"The White Lotus."

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:12.167
Take a look at this.

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:13.834
-I don't want a free massage.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:16.634
I don't want cheap champagne.

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:20.400
What I want is
to speak to your boss.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.501
-Well, I am the resort manager.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:24.300
-Yeah, but you have a boss.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.868
Who is your boss?

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:29.501
-Our general manager, Mr. Zeoli,
is at a conference this week.

00:06:29.501 --> 00:06:32.100
-Yeah, I want to
get in touch with him.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.968
Can I have his number?
-I'll have him call you.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:37.701
-No! No. I'm calling him.

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:40.801
-I will have someone
bring you his business card

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.834
with his cellphone number
to your room,

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:44.701
and you can call him
at your leisure.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:45.734
-Good.

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:48.667
This morning, please.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.667
♪♪

00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:58.868
-Mother[bleep]

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:03.667
-That is how you
do it right there.

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:07.133
Murray Bartlett. Home run.

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:08.701
-Thank you.
-Fantastic.

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:11.434
"The White Lotus"
is streaming now on HBO Max.

00:07:11.434 --> 00:07:14.133
Check out Season 2 of
"Physical" on Apple TV+.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.434
Demi Lovato
performs after the break.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:17.968
Stick around!
[ Cheers and applause ]

